{"authored" [{"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨{e}^{3t},\\,{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "257c0973d947c8f23c6217a25f46489063f0328f4c9b0fe067119336381a6ee3" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+1),1-{t}^{2}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+1)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{3t+1},-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨\\frac{3}{3(2)+1},-2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "257c0973d947c8f23c6217a25f46489063f0328f4c9b0fe067119336381a6ee3" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{5},-7⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,-7⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡7,-4⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/state.json" "file_sha256" "8e4778f423c7ccd33fdeb4430ad4f0dfa53aab42f2c54834f8ada05112ae6bfc" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 12t+t^2, t^3+1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-620.json" "file_sha256" "2f132021883704af282fdbf195421c6a5d99b6f7e15c7f5b5174c0788815b00d" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t+{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12+2t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-620.json" "file_sha256" "2f132021883704af282fdbf195421c6a5d99b6f7e15c7f5b5174c0788815b00d" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle,$ measured in $\\textrm{m}/\\textrm s,$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds, is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t^4-t^2, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-7224.json" "file_sha256" "acf774ade0883801d551d1707393539d8bc2eaaa37a49523c15b8c5dd262f4c5" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3}-2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3}-2(1),6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(1)|\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨2,6⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-7224.json" "file_sha256" "acf774ade0883801d551d1707393539d8bc2eaaa37a49523c15b8c5dd262f4c5" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 4t^2+1, 3t^2-t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-621.json" "file_sha256" "3307328c4b2685bff66973fdd74883efb3d52ec913eb0c08d5232e7a6d573dc2" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector. We can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8t,\\,6t-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-621.json" "file_sha256" "3307328c4b2685bff66973fdd74883efb3d52ec913eb0c08d5232e7a6d573dc2" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $\\mathbf{r},$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\left\\langle t^{5}-t^2,\\, t^2+6t-3 \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-7225.json" "file_sha256" "fd0bac72666dcf112b83c723db87c73576b28a5dc37e352e7adc089cf423a925" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-7225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{5}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6t-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5{t}^{4}-2t,\\,2t+6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+6)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨20{t}^{3}-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨20(0)^{3}-2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(0)|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨-2,\\,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/example-7225.json" "file_sha256" "fd0bac72666dcf112b83c723db87c73576b28a5dc37e352e7adc089cf423a925" "basis" 1466 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040802/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨{e}^{3t},\\,{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351111" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3e^{3t}"] "category" "ma_successful_gra