105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-4t+8),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\,10t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-351105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351105" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351105" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨3{t}^{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2},\\,-t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=3,$ we substitute $t=3$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =⟨9(3)^{2},\\,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9\\cdot 9,\\,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨81,\\,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(3)=⟨27,\\,-3⟩"] ["math" "a(3)=⟨27,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "a(3)=⟨81,\\,-3⟩"] ["math" "a(3)=⟨81,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "a(3)=⟨9,\\,-3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-6392" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(3)=⟨81,\\,-3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds, is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨6t+1,-3{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨6,-6(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨-6,6⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+({6}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot 36} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{52}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+1),1-{t}^{2}⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t+1)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{3t+1},-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨\\frac{3}{3(2)+1},-2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{5},-7⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-2⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡3,-7⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡7,-4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121919" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨\\frac{3}{7},-4⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨2{t}^{2}-4t,5t-{t}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t-4,\\,5-3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨4(2)-4,\\,5-3(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8-4,\\,5-12⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(2)=⟨0,-7⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨0,2⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨4,-3⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨4,-7⟩"] ["math" "a(2)=⟨4,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(2)=⟨4,-7⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $v=⟨u,v⟩,$ measured in $\\text{m}/\\text{s},$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}^{2}+2t,6{t}^{2}-3⟩.\n$$\n\nFind the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+2,\\,12t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨2(0)+2,12(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨2,0⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "16\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "3\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31674" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-2t,\\,{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-2,\\,4{t}^{3}-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t,\\,12{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12t^2-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨3{t}^{3}+t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{3}+t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9{t}^{2}+1,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=⟨18,\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨18t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨18t,\\,-\\frac{2}{t}⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨9{t}^{2}+1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨9{t}^{2}+1,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-85606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=⟨18t,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4{t}^{3}-21,2{t}^{4}+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-21),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}+3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{2},\\,8{t}^{3}+3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24t,\\,24{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da