xt{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(9{t}^{2}-12t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+17)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18t-12,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(18t-12),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨18,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-7161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=⟨18,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨18t-12,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨9,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨9,\\,4⟩"] ["math" "a=⟨9t,\\,4⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-7161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=⟨18,\\,0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r(t)$ of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{t}^{2}(t-2),\\,t(3-t)⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the components of the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t.$\n\n$a=⟨${{field-1}},{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}(t-2)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t(3-t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-4t,\\,3-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6t-4,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6t-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-347194" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5,\\,{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{t}^{1/2}+8t,\\,3{t}^{2}-8t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{1/2}+8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-8t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{-1/2}+8,\\,6t-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨3(1)^{-1/2}+8,\\,6(1)-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+8,\\,6-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨11,\\,-2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),2{t}^{4}+3⟩,\\,t>0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}+3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t+1},8{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t+1}),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(t+1)^{2}},24{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(1+1)^{2}},24({1}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{4},24⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a(1)=⟨-\\frac{1}{2},24⟩"] ["math" "a(1)=⟨-\\frac{1}{4},12⟩"] ["math" "a(1)=⟨-\\frac{1}{4},24⟩"] ["math" "a(1)=⟨\\frac{1}{2},12⟩"] ["math" "a(1)=⟨\\frac{1}{2},16⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-121936" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a(1)=⟨-\\frac{1}{4},24⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+3,\\,{t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+1⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe magnitude of the acceleration is\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-3{t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15{t}^{2}-4t,\\,4{t}^{3}-6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-6t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30t-4,\\,12{t}^{2}-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(2) & =⟨30(2)-4,\\,12(2)^{2}-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨60-4,\\,48-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨56,\\,42⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(2)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(2)| & =|⟨56,\\,42⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{56}^{2}+{42}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3136+1764} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4900} \\\\  & =70\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the acceleration at time $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is $70{\\text{ m/s}}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-351408" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-351408" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "70"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{4}{1+t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-4t+5⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{1+t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-4t+5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{(1+t)^{2}},\\,{t}^{2}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{4}{(1+t)^{2}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{(1+t)^{3}},\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨\\frac{8}{(1+(1))^{3}},\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{{2}^{3}},\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨1,\\,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "2\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82337" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $r,$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+5t,\\,2{t}^{4}-4{t}^{2}+t+1⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}+5t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-4{t}^{2}+t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{t}^{2}+6t+5,\\,8{t}^{3}-8t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+6t+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-8t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12t+6,\\,24{t}^{2}-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨12(0)+6,\\,24(0)-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(0)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨6,\\,-8⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c439abc6883a4f52d0bd42ea0cda5d833848215aa1a4c9b36a353704806da4c3"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "6\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] ["math" "8\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "q-82336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/state.json" "file_sha256" "be782deea12100a9b59bcc7185bee9f050a79fc9afb0fe21b2a5714ff0cfc77d"} {"question" "e-620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 12t+t^2, t^3+1\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-620.json" "file_sha256" "ee94cc9c41d9e42597dbc1d7e6c974a5a455d56e5f50cc92638796fc0f1b177a"} {"question" "e-620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12t+{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12+2t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-620.json" "file_sha256" "ee94cc9c41d9e42597dbc1d7e6c974a5a455d56e5f50cc92638796fc0f1b177a"} {"question" "e-7224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The velocity vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle u, v \\rangle,$ measured in $\\textrm{m}/\\textrm s,$ of a particle $P$ at time $t$ seconds, is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t^4-t^2, 2t^3\\rangle.\n$$\n\nFind the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-7224.json" "file_sha256" "a9444baecb3e841f2e979a4f71541c4e5495c2916e2397d2186f3f517afc6c71"} {"question" "e-7224" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3}-2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨4(1)^{3}-2(1),6(1)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(1)|\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨2,6⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-7224.json" "file_sha256" "a9444baecb3e841f2e979a4f71541c4e5495c2916e2397d2186f3f517afc6c71"} {"question" "e-621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $\\mathbf{r}$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 4t^2+1, 3t^2-t\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $\\mathbf{a}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-621.json" "file_sha256" "ece3cc8f61bcdf3bb781b9ba5b1734f3cbed912aa41fdac53f018967d2c54a11"} {"question" "e-621" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector. We can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8t,\\,6t-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-621.json" "file_sha256" "ece3cc8f61bcdf3bb781b9ba5b1734f3cbed912aa41fdac53f018967d2c54a11"} {"question" "e-7225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The position vector $\\mathbf{r},$ in meters, of a particle $P$ relative to a fixed origin $O$ at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\left\\langle t^{5}-t^2,\\, t^2+6t-3 \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector and the magnitude of the acceleration of $P$ at time $t=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-7225.json" "file_sha256" "c5fd46246094ebc6cdfc387580aa8405db8b9b5f7e60cc997ca6d2620cee4d4f"} {"question" "e-7225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{5}-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+6t-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5{t}^{4}-2t,\\,2t+6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{4}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+6)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨20{t}^{3}-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=0,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =⟨20(0)^{3}-2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|\\mathbf a(0)|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(0)| & =|⟨-2,\\,2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/example-7225.json" "file_sha256" "c5fd46246094ebc6cdfc387580aa8405db8b9b5f7e60cc997ca6d2620cee4d4f"} {"question" "q-31683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}^{2}"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062885/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "5ffb6832af9928120fbb58da98fa0e45d88bfeca13c7fa757026be24a3f68704" "reviewer_session" "01a11908-fa8d-7c61-8e03-c1185d0b9506" "rationale" "Twice differentiating gives a(t)=⟨3t^(-1/2)+8,6t−8⟩, so a(1)=⟨11,−2⟩ and its magnitude is sqrt(125)=5sqrt(5) meters per second squared. Original option a and the authentic solution visibly use m/s², and saved grading reports Correct. The derived capture {\\text{m/s}}² incorrectly squares the meter unit as well. Correct that serialization in all five original choices without changing their coefficients." "bindings" {"problem" "3ae40abc0264386dcfc29ef2675d4caa520a65d85448b44c0043bf901bff2a22" "worked_solution" "ee7c69fe6d0443fa18435f09b07186f606472c7c734158ef76a6d7525b831251" "original_field" "56b7e2829f06be1ab112903be723c892fbf685fa234af4590529e5b6e9f85975" "reviewed_field" "24c8f8b0761ffb0fd2415e06fc63785ebdaeb7c6176b479c457340798bf81a07" "raw_widget" "a0e60aee12df43ab1cb71149956294cf5ef74926e2308691588dd9ae1a45ae67"} "evidence_files" [{"path" "q-31683-before.png" "sha256" "3964c8ace7953681783fa58ea514fe4821b9b6ab1e6e78d1748800e0d6e3cedc"} {"path" "q-31683-before.json" "sha256" "f4502c3343a8f28b8f1560fff2ca633428a2923c201587e6ff57369db990d718"} {"path" "history-q-31683.png" "sha256" "c5cddb741a82430200f2d2d6a64cb198ee1edf5f4cd946321754863fa4349e9b"} {"path" "q-31683-after.json" "sha256" "2844e8825001c93294de1b440479aa8cced7df48776630d532eb553b77f46e17"} {"path" "edb-import/questions.edn" "sha256" "5f0865418c1b4c0531dd54fa70bb3d3ebb2388b694a36a57a683867bb8